Given the weight of the legal precedents cited in this document,
I am surprised that the CIA even presented its motion to dismiss.
Were they unaware of the precedents?  If so, why?  Wouldn't it
be reasonable to assume that a government agency as large
as the CIA would have lawyers who are reasonable knowledgeable
about case histories to know that they would receive this type
of response?  If the answer is yes, then they made a frivilous
